# Who owns what in this repository (M192, ADR-0024, decision D177).
#
# The LAST matching line wins, as GitHub reads it. This file is read twice: by GitHub, to request a
# review from the owners, and by CI's boundary step (scripts/boundary-check.php), which reads it from
# the BASE commit and refuses a pull request that changes another owner's paths without that owner's
# `boundary-approved` label. "Require review from code owners" is deliberately OFF on `main`: with one
# owner per side, an author could never approve their own pull request.
#
# The working agreement both developers follow is docs/working-agreement.md.

